--  A server that a new version of its program can take over from (ADR
--  0032). The old version answers it, and only the new one calls it,
--  which mem launches with this interface as its Previous argument (#865,
--  #866). State and Caps don't change the old version, so that it
--  carries on as it was if the handover fails, and either may be called
--  any number of times.
--
--  State is the old version's state as a stream, starting with a format
--  version (Rose.Replacement writes and reads it). Caps is the caps that
--  the old version holds, in a fresh set, each named in the state. Each
--  is the caller's to release when it is done with it.
--
--  Replies is the reply caps of the calls that the old version has
--  deferred, which the state lists, in a fresh set (#879). A reply cap is
--  moved, not copied (#864), so they are given out once, and Replies
--  raises if they are out already. The old version keeps a cap to the
--  set: whichever version next serves a call takes them from it, which is
--  the new version once it has taken over, and the old one if the
--  handover failed. Releasing the set before then fails the calls.

interface Replaceable is

   function State
     return interface Releasable_Reader;

   function Caps
     return interface Releasable_Cap_Set;

   function Replies
     return interface Releasable_Cap_Set;

end Replaceable;
